4</fpage>&#x02013;1170, <year>2005</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15793257</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r10"><label>10</label><citation citation-type="journal">Donmoyer CM, Chen SS, Hande SA, Lacy DB, Ejiofor J, McGuinness OP: Hyperinsulinemia compensates for infection-induced impairment in net hepatic glucose uptake during TPN. <source>Am J Physiol Endocrinol Metab</source> <volume>279</volume>: <fpage>E235</fpage>&#x02013;E243, <year>2000</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10913021</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r11"><label>11</label><citation citation-type="journal">Galassetti P, Koyama Y, Coker RH, Lacy DB, Cherrington AD, Wasserman DH: Role of a negative arterial-portal venous glucose gradient in the postexercise state. <source>Am J Physiol</source> <volume>277</volume>: <fpage>E1038</fpage>&#x02013;E1045, <year>1999</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10600793</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r12"><label>12</label><citation citation-type="journal">Moore MC, Hsieh PS, Neal DW, Cherrington AD: Nonhepatic response to portal glucose delivery in conscious dogs. <source>Am J Physiol Endocrinol Metab</source> <volume>279</volume>: <fpage>E1271</fpage>&#x02013;E1277, <year>2000</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11093914</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r13"><label>13</label><citation citation-type="journal">Meier JJ, Nauck MA: The potential role of glucagon-like peptide 1 in diabetes. <source>Curr Opin Investig Drugs</source> <volume>5</volume>: <fpage>402</fpage>&#x02013;410, <year>2004</year></citation></ref><ref id="r14"><label>14</label><citation citation-type="journal">Mari A, Sallas WM, He YL, Watson C, Ligueros-Saylan M, Dunning BE, Deacon CF, Holst JJ, Foley JE: Vildagliptin, a dipeptidyl peptidase-IV inhibitor, improves model-assessed beta-cell function in patients with type 2 diabetes. <source>J Clin Endocrinol Metab</source> <volume>90</volume>: <fpage>4888</fpage>&#x02013;4894, <year>2005</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15886245</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r15"><label>15</label><citation citation-type="journal">Ionut V, Hucking K, Liberty IF, Bergman RN: Synergistic effect of portal glucose and glucagon-like peptide-1 to lower systemic glucose and stimulate counter-regulatory hormones. <source>Diabetologia</source> <volume>48</volume>: <fpage>967</fpage>&#x02013;975, <year>2005</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15830188</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r16"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="journal">Johnson KM, Edgerton DS, Rodewald T, Scott M, Farmer B, Neal D, Cherrington AD: Intraportal GLP-1 infusion increases nonhepatic glucose utilization without changing pancreatic hormone levels. <source>Am J Physiol Endocrinol Metab</source> <volume>293</volume>: <fpage>E1085</fpage>&#x02013;E1091, <year>2007</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17684104</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r17"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="journal">Ahren B, Holst JJ, Martensson H, Balkan B: Improved glucose tolerance and insulin secretion by inhibition of dipeptidyl peptidase IV in mice. <source>Eur J Pharmacol</source> <volume>404</volume>: <fpage>239</fpage>&#x02013;245, <year>2000</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10980284</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r18"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal">Drucker DJ: Enhancing incretin action for the treatment of type 2 diabetes. <source>Diabetes Care</source> <volume>26</volume>: <fpage>2929</fpage>&#x02013;2940, <year>2003</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14514604</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r19"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="journal">Ahren B, Thomaseth K, Pacini G: Reduced insulin clearance contributes to the increased insulin levels after administration of glucagon-like peptide 1 in mice. <source>Diabetologia</source> <volume>48</volume>: <fpage>2140</fpage>&#x02013;2146, <year>2005</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16132949</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r20"><label>20</label><citation citation-type="journal">Groop PH, Groop L, Totterman KJ, Fyhrquist F: Relationship between changes in GIP concentrations and changes in insulin and C-peptide concentrations after guar gum therapy. <source>Scand J Clin Lab Invest</source> <volume>46</volume>: <fpage>505</fpage>&#x02013;510, <year>1986</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3535000</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r21"><label>21</label><citation citation-type="journal">Kindmark H, Pigon J, Efendic S: Glucose-dependent insulinotropic hormone potentiates the hypoglycemic effect of glibenclamide in healthy volunteers: evidence for an effect on insulin extraction. <source>J Clin Endocrinol Metab</source> <volume>86</volume>: <fpage>2015</fpage>&#x02013;2019, <year>2001</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11344200</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r22"><label>22</label><citation citation-type="journal">Rudovich NN, Rochlitz HJ, Pfeiffer AF: Reduced hepatic insulin extraction in response to gastric inhibitory polypeptide compensates for reduced insulin secretion in normal-weight and normal glucose tolerant first-degree relatives of type 2 diabetic patients. <source>Diabetes</source> <volume>53</volume>: <fpage>2359</fpage>&#x02013;2365, <year>2004</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15331546</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r23"><label>23</label><citation citation-type="journal">Brandt A, Katschinski M, Arnold R, Polonsky KS, Goke B, Byrne MM: GLP-1-induced alterations in the glucose-stimulated insulin secretory dose-response curve. <source>Am J Physiol Endocrinol Metab</source> <volume>281</volume>: <fpage>E242</fpage>&#x02013;E247, <year>2001</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11440899</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r24"><label>24</label><citation citation-type="journal">Hanks JB, Andersen DK, Wise JE, Putnam WS, Meyers WC, Jones RS: The hepatic extraction of gastric inhibitory polypeptide and insulin. <source>Endocrinology</source> <volume>115</volume>: <fpage>1011</fpage>&#x02013;1018, <year>1984</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">6378600</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r25"><label>25</label><citation citation-type="journal">Meier JJ, Gallwitz B, Siepmann N, Holst JJ, Deacon CF, Schmidt WE, Nauck MA: The reduction in hepatic insulin clearance after oral glucose is not mediated by gastric inhibitory polypeptide (GIP). <source>Regul Pept</source> <volume>113</volume>: <fpage>95</fpage>&#x02013;100, <year>2003</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12686467</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r26"><label>26</label><citation citation-type="journal">Meier JJ, Holst JJ, Schmidt WE, Nauck MA: Reduction of hepatic insulin clearance after oral glucose ingestion is not mediated by glucagon-like peptide 1 or gastric inhibitory polypeptide in humans. <source>Am J Physiol Endocrinol Metab</source> <volume>293</volume>: <fpage>E849</fpage>&#x02013;E856, <year>2007</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17609256</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r27"><label>27</label><citation citation-type="journal">Ionut V, Liberty IF, Hucking K, Lottati M, Stefanovski D, Zheng D, Bergman RN: Exogenously imposed postprandial-like rises in systemic glucose and GLP-1 do not produce an incretin effect, suggesting an indirect mechanism of GLP-1 action. <source>Am J Physiol Endocrinol Metab</source> <volume>291</volume>: <fpage>E779</fpage>&#x02013;E785, <year>2006</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16720628</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r28"><label>28</label><citation citation-type="journal">Kawai K, Suzuki S, Ohashi S, Mukai H, Ohmori H, Murayama Y, Yamashita K: Comparison of the effects of glucagon-like peptide-1-(1-37) and -(7-37) and glucagon on islet hormone release from isolated perfused canine and rat pancreases. <source>Endocrinology</source> <volume>124</volume>: <fpage>1768</fpage>&#x02013;1773, <year>1989</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2564338</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r29"><label>29</label><citation citation-type="journal">van der Burg MP, Guicherit OR, Frolich M, Gooszen HG: Insulinotropic effects of cholecystokinin, gastric inhibitory poly